{"name":"Sasquatch Socks","hex":"#ff4681","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sasquatch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large hairy humanoid creature of western North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sasquatch"},{"term":"socks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of sock"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of sock"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/socks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bigfoot","blocks":[{"text":"Bigfoot, or Sasquatch, is a large, hairy, mythical humanoid creature said to inhabit forests in North America, particularly in the Pacific Northwest. Bigfoot is featured in both American and Canadian folklore, and since the mid-20th century has become a cultural icon, permeating popular culture and becoming the subject of its own distinct subculture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg/330px-Patterson_Gimlin_Bigfoot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot","wikidata":"Q44810"},{"title":"Sock","blocks":[{"text":"A sock is a piece of clothing worn on the feet and often covering the ankle or some part of the calf. Some types of shoes or boots are typically worn over socks. In ancient times, socks were made from leather or matted animal hair. Machine-knit socks were first produced in the late 16th century. Until the 1800s, both hand-made and machine-knit socks were manufactured, with the latter technique becoming more common in the 19th century, and continuing until the modern day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/HandKnittedWhiteLaceSock.jpg/330px-HandKnittedWhiteLaceSock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sock","wikidata":"Q43663"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or